:: Prototype Test-Run Preparation [event main_quest] {"position":"3025,250","size":"100,100"}
I lean back from the desk and stare at the screen for a full minute before I let myself believe it. The thing runs. It's held together with electrical tape and about four hundred if-statements, and I still have to babysit half its parameters by hand, but it runs, and it might actually be ready for a real test.

The question is who to test it on. This version can't do much by itself yet. It needs a profile, a set of numbers tuned to one specific person, which rules out strangers. It has to be someone I know inside out, so $mom.callName or $sister.callName. If something goes wrong, I'm also the one person who could talk his way out of it with them.

Then there's the question of what to ask. It can't be anything huge. It has to be something they'd never do just because I asked, but might do on their own on a good day... I catch myself grinning at the ceiling before I've even finished the thought. $mom.callName. Some time to herself, alone in her own bed, the kind she probably hasn't allowed herself in years. Nobody gets hurt and nobody ever finds out. And if she actually goes through with it, I'll know the prototype works.

If it fails, I have no idea how I'd explain that conversation. I decide not to think about that part too hard. <<if $mom.stats.relation < 10>>First, though, she needs to trust me a little more. Right now she'd laugh me out of the room.<</if>>

